CREA v2  —  n8n Hands Layer
2.0.0 · 2026-09-09

A standalone, client-owned automation pack: a WhatsApp AI booking assistant plus the
shoot-ops automations (Acuity intake, confirmations, chase, card pipeline, invoicing,
morning briefing, listing leads).

Install: INSTALL.md   (one runbook, ~1 hour, mostly account signups + downloads)
Deploy:  ./go-live.sh (Docker Compose — n8n + WAHA + vault-api, one command)

What v2 is
- Runs entirely under the buyer's own accounts and their own Mac. No shared services, no
  public URL, no tunnel. WhatsApp reaches n8n on a private Docker network; Acuity is polled
  outbound every 10 minutes.
- The conversation state store and alert sink are folded into vault-api; the pack ships its
  own error workflow (crea-00).
- CREA_VAULT_DIR points booking storage at the buyer's Obsidian vault so Obsidian Sync backs
  it up and puts it on their phone. See DATA-AND-BACKUP.md.
- One command brings the whole stack up, imports every workflow, creates the credentials and
  activates everything. The only manual step is scanning the WhatsApp QR once.

Verified 2026-09-09 against a live model on n8n 2.30.7: answered from the knowledge file
($450 quoted verbatim, nothing invented), checked availability without confirming a slot,
captured the shoot brief across turns, handed the owner a quote-ready enquiry, wrote the lead
note; multi-turn routing holds under fast consecutive messages; the Acuity poller ingests new
bookings and dedupes on a watermark; LLM-down falls through to the deterministic qualifier;
card-pipeline human gate and the error handler reach their designed end.

Not fully verified on the build machine: the Docker Compose bring-up itself (the build Mac
ran out of disk). Confirmed: `docker compose config` resolves; go-live.sh's preflight, key
generation, workflow fill and clean-env steps all run; the WhatsApp-gateway image is
amd64-only on its default tag, so go-live.sh now picks `devlikeapro/waha:noweb` /
`:noweb-arm` by CPU architecture. `./go-live.sh --test` is the on-site acceptance check.
